        "eventMetadata": {
          "context_description": "Xi Jinping\u2019s entrenched control over the Chinese Communist Party, military, and state institutions underpins the overwhelming trader consensus against his departure before 2027. Since abolishing presidential term limits in 2018, he has conducted repeated purges of senior officials and generals to neutralize potential rivals, installed loyalists in key posts ahead of the 21st Party Congress, and shown no public signals of stepping aside. Recent diplomatic activity, including the late-August 2026 Shanghai Cooperation Organization summit, and positioning of allies for continued leadership roles further signal continuity. While opaque health observations occasionally surface, no verified developments indicate imminent removal. Unexpected shifts could still arise from a sudden medical event or rapid elite realignment, though structural barriers remain substantial.",
          "context_requires_regen": true,
